<h2>2. Organization Vision</h2>
<div class="highlight-box">
  <em>"XYZ E-commerce Solutions Inc. aims to be a leader in the e-commerce industry by leveraging technology to streamline operations, optimize inventory management, and enhance customer satisfaction through real-time operational visibility and robust automated replenishment."</em>
</div>

<h2>3. Project Objectives (SMART)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Specific:</strong> Develop and implement a comprehensive, cloud-native web-based Inventory Management System (IMS) for XYZ E-commerce Solutions Inc. to streamline inventory tracking, supplier management, purchase order processing, automated stock alerting, and multi-tier reporting.</li>
  <li><strong>Measurable:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Reduce inventory stockouts by <strong>80%</strong>.</li>
      <li>Achieve <strong>98% accuracy</strong> in real-time inventory records.</li>
      <li>Improve supplier delivery performance by <strong>25%</strong>.</li>
      <li>Increase user adoption rate to <strong>90%</strong> within 3 months of system deployment.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Attainable:</strong> Allocate a dedicated cross-functional team (1 Project Manager, 1 Business Analyst, 1 UX/UI Designer, 1 Tech Lead, 4 Full-Stack Developers, 1 QA Lead, 2 QA Engineers, 1 DevOps Engineer). Utilize modern tech stack: Java 21, Spring Boot 3.3.3, Angular 18+, Oracle 19c / TiDB Cloud, and Docker.</li>
  <li><strong>Relevant:</strong> Directly aligns with XYZ E-commerce Solutions Inc.'s strategy to eliminate manual supply chain bottlenecks, stock discrepancy, and purchase order delays.</li>
  <li><strong>Time-Bound:</strong> Complete development, testing, cloud deployment, and user acceptance validation within <strong>20 calendar days</strong>.</li>
</ul>

