<h2>5. Existing Challenges Faced by the Client</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Inefficient Manual Inventory Tracking:</strong> Spreadsheets and paper logs led to frequent stockouts on fast-moving goods and costly overstocking of slow-moving inventory.</li>
  <li><strong>Lack of Supplier Visibility:</strong> No centralized system to monitor supplier lead times, delivery reliability scores, or historical defective shipment rates.</li>
  <li><strong>Manual & Error-Prone Purchase Order Processing:</strong> Purchase orders created via emails or paper resulted in misplaced items, inaccurate quantities, and duplicate invoices.</li>
  <li><strong>Limited Reporting & Analytics:</strong> Executive management lacked real-time visibility into stock valuation, inventory turnover ratio, and pending shipments across different warehouse facilities.</li>
</ol>

<h2>6. Need for Adopting Agile Methodology</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width:25%;">Key Agile Tenet</th>
    <th style="width:38%;">Quantitative Benefits</th>
    <th style="width:37%;">Qualitative Benefits</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Customer collaboration over contract negotiation</strong></td>
    <td>• 25% increase in stakeholder satisfaction ratings via continuous review demos.<br>• 30% reduction in change requests and post-delivery rework.</td>
    <td>Enhanced trust and partnership between development engineers and warehouse operations teams; accurate capture of operational nuances.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Responding to change over following a plan</strong></td>
    <td>• 20% improved time-to-market for critical warehouse features.<br>• 15% reduction in wasted development effort by prioritizing highest-value epics.</td>
    <td>High flexibility to adjust to emerging supply chain constraints, new supplier APIs, and fluctuating operational priorities.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Working software over comprehensive documentation</strong></td>
    <td>• 25% accelerated delivery of functional increments across 5-day sprint cycles.<br>• 20% reduction in documentation maintenance overhead.</td>
    <td>High confidence from stakeholders who interacted with live deployed prototypes on Render at the end of each sprint.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Individuals and interactions over processes and tools</strong></td>
    <td>• 15% boost in engineering velocity through daily standups and pair programming.<br>• 10% lower turnover through clear ownership and blameless post-mortems.</td>
    <td>Fosters proactive problem-solving, rapid bug resolution, and high morale across development and QA teams.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>7. Scope of the Project & Core Modules</h2>
<p><strong>Type of Work:</strong> Full-Stack Custom Software Development (Web-Based Application)<br>
<strong>Implementation Strategy:</strong> Custom development from scratch using a decoupled micro-ready architecture (Angular SPA + Spring Boot REST API + Relational Database).</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Module 1: Stock Tracking & Real-Time Alerts:</strong> Real-time stock levels, multi-warehouse bin tracking, adjustment audits, and automated low-stock / out-of-stock triggers.</li>
  <li><strong>Module 2: Supplier Management:</strong> Supplier registry, contact directory, lead-time tracking, and quality performance scoring.</li>
  <li><strong>Module 3: Purchase Order Processing:</strong> Automated PO creation, supplier assignment, line item tracking, delivery date tracking, and status progression (CREATED, APPROVED, DELIVERED).</li>
  <li><strong>Module 4: Inventory Reporting & Analytics:</strong> Executive dashboards, stock valuation, inventory turnover analytics, CSV report generation, and consolidated financial summaries.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Epics in Scope & User Stories</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width:22%;">Epic</th>
    <th style="width:12%;">Duration</th>
    <th style="width:40%;">User Story</th>
    <th style="width:26%;">Key Deliverables</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Stock Tracking & Alerts</strong></td>
    <td>5 Days</td>
    <td><em>As a warehouse manager, I want to track real-time inventory levels and receive alerts for low stock levels so that I can initiate procurement in a timely manner.</em></td>
    <td>Inventory ledger, multi-warehouse stock allocations, view_low_inventory_alerts, view_out_of_stock_alerts.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Supplier Management</strong></td>
    <td>4 Days</td>
    <td><em>As a procurement officer, I want to manage supplier information and track supplier performance so that I can optimize vendor selection.</em></td>
    <td>Supplier master directory, performance evaluation metrics, lead-time tracking, REST CRUD endpoints.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Purchase Order Processing</strong></td>
    <td>5 Days</td>
    <td><em>As a purchasing officer, I want to create and track purchase orders for required materials so that I can ensure timely procurement and maintain inventory levels.</em></td>
    <td>PO requisition wizard, line item calculations, status progression workflow (CREATED ➔ APPROVED ➔ DELIVERED).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Inventory Reporting & Analytics</strong></td>
    <td>4 Days</td>
    <td><em>As a business analyst, I want to access comprehensive inventory reports and dashboards so that I can gain insights into stock levels and turnover.</em></td>
    <td>Consolidated financial reporting, multi-currency conversion, CSV export engine, real-time database viewer.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>9. Technology Stack</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width:25%;">Layer</th>
    <th style="width:30%;">Technology</th>
    <th style="width:45%;">Details</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Front-End</strong></td>
    <td>Angular 18+, HTML5, CSS3, TypeScript</td>
    <td>Standalone components, reactive RxJS state management, responsive UI without heavy CSS framework bloat.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Back-End</strong></td>
    <td>Java 21 LTS, Spring Boot 3.3.3</td>
    <td>Spring Web MVC, Spring Security 6 with stateless JWT, Spring Data JPA / Hibernate, Flyway Database Migrations.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Database</strong></td>
    <td>Oracle 19c & TiDB Cloud Serverless</td>
    <td>57 normalized relational tables, ACID transaction semantics, foreign key integrity, dual SQL compatibility scripts provided.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>DevOps & Cloud</strong></td>
    <td>Docker, Render.com, GitHub Actions</td>
    <td>Multi-stage Docker builds (Alpine Linux, Nginx reverse proxy), automated CI/CD pipeline, SSL/TLS encryption.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Testing</strong></td>
    <td>JUnit 5, Mockito, Postman, Jest</td>
    <td>Automated unit tests, integration tests for API endpoints, end-to-end user acceptance validation.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

